.nh
.TH "PB-APPROVE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-approve - Approve a peer machine over gRPC IPC


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb approve <machine-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Approve a peer machine over gRPC IPC

.PP
Approve an exact peer machine ID for local access. Inspect the ID before approving an unfamiliar peer. Withdrawing a machine is \fBpb machine revoke\fR, which asks for confirmation; pb approve never revokes.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for approve

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
